WEBVTT

1
00:00:09.362 --> 00:00:11.643
getting a babysitter tonight," Dad said.

2
00:00:11.663 --> 00:00:13.685
"I don't need one.

3
00:00:14.065 --> 00:00:16.347
I'm not a baby," I complained.

4
00:00:16.367 --> 00:00:19.749
"Sorry, Bobby," Mom said.

5
00:00:19.769 --> 00:00:23.251
"We can't leave you home alone at night."

6
00:00:23.272 --> 00:00:26.774
"Fine," I grumbled.

7
00:00:26.794 --> 00:00:29.396
"When will Carla get here?"

8
00:00:31.076 --> 00:00:33.957
"Carla has a softball game tonight," Dad said.

9
00:00:33.977 --> 00:00:37.519
"Mrs. Muller will babysit you instead."

10
00:00:37.539 --> 00:00:40.100
"Oh no!"

11
00:00:40.800 --> 00:00:41.261
I thought.

12
00:00:41.281 --> 00:00:42.961
"She's scary!"

13
00:00:50.385 --> 00:00:51.625
Mrs. Muller arrived.

14
00:00:51.645 --> 00:00:56.888
"The first aid kit is in the closet," Mom said.

15
00:00:57.924 --> 00:01:00.745
"There's a list of emergency phone numbers on the counter.

16
00:01:00.965 --> 00:01:02.846
Bobby doesn't have any food allergies.

17
00:01:02.926 --> 00:01:04.206
And his bedtime is at ten."

18
00:01:06.347 --> 00:01:07.467
Mom and Dad left.

19
00:01:07.487 --> 00:01:11.948
"Did you finish your homework?"

20
00:01:12.308 --> 00:01:13.469
Mrs. Muller asked.

21
00:01:14.469 --> 00:01:17.230
"No. Tomorrow is Saturday," I said.

22
00:01:17.250 --> 00:01:21.511
"No excuses," she said sternly.

23
00:01:21.531 --> 00:01:23.512
"Go get started."

24
00:01:32.348 --> 00:01:34.950
A little while later I went into the kitchen.

25
00:01:34.970 --> 00:01:37.311
"What's for dinner?"

26
00:01:37.751 --> 00:01:38.271
I asked.

27
00:01:39.292 --> 00:01:40.473
"Turkey burgers!"

28
00:01:40.733 --> 00:01:41.333
she said.

29
00:01:41.353 --> 00:01:46.056
"And I don't want to hear any complaints!"

30
00:01:51.319 --> 00:01:53.600
After dinner I asked to watch TV.

31
00:01:53.620 --> 00:01:55.941
"Sure," Mrs.

32
00:01:56.001 --> 00:01:56.702
Muller said.

33
00:01:56.722 --> 00:02:00.344
"We'll watch my favorite show."

34
00:02:03.360 --> 00:02:06.343
"It's probably something boring," I thought.

35
00:02:09.825 --> 00:02:12.327
She flicked through the TV channels.

36
00:02:14.369 --> 00:02:16.531
Then she stopped at channel ten.

37
00:02:17.732 --> 00:02:19.113
Space Rangers was on.

38
00:02:20.514 --> 00:02:21.755
I looked at her in surprise.

39
00:02:21.775 --> 00:02:24.557
"This is your favorite show too?"

40
00:02:24.577 --> 00:02:26.539
"Of course!"

41
00:02:26.959 --> 00:02:27.500
she said.

42
00:02:32.103 --> 00:02:33.536
After the show Mrs.

43
00:02:33.596 --> 00:02:35.257
Muller pointed to my video games.

44
00:02:35.277 --> 00:02:39.420
"Do you have Super Ninja?"

45
00:02:39.760 --> 00:02:40.380
she asked.

46
00:02:40.400 --> 00:02:43.542
"Wow! You play video games?"

47
00:02:44.022 --> 00:02:44.522
I asked.

48
00:02:44.542 --> 00:02:49.165
"I play them with my grandson," she said.

49
00:02:49.185 --> 00:02:51.947
"And watch out.

50
00:02:51.967 --> 00:02:53.788
I usually win!"

51
00:03:03.988 --> 00:03:05.969
Soon it was ten o'clock.

52
00:03:08.309 --> 00:03:10.670
"Time flies," she said.

53
00:03:10.690 --> 00:03:13.171
"It's your bedtime."

54
00:03:14.991 --> 00:03:15.691
I sighed.

55
00:03:15.711 --> 00:03:19.112
"Hmm," Mrs.

56
00:03:19.172 --> 00:03:19.872
Muller said.

57
00:03:19.892 --> 00:03:24.053
"I guess one more game wouldn't hurt."

58
00:03:24.073 --> 00:03:29.475
"Can you be my babysitter next time?"

59
00:03:29.975 --> 00:03:30.475
I asked.

60
00:03:31.816 --> 00:03:34.325
Mrs. Muller nodded, "Sure."

61
00:03:34.865 --> 00:03:36.907
She even smiled at me.

62
00:03:38.148 --> 00:03:40.610
Mrs. Muller wasn't scary after all.
